title ALES12 — Lotus's equal-power crossfade, the same law swept over time
prompt Continue the autonomous recur (baton prin recur): next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, STOP only at custody gates.
think Eighth increment of this recur, the second full round this turn (after ALES11 equal-power pan landed and pushed). No custody gate in reach — the Lotus ladder is pure local software.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the most durable next thing is not a NEW law but the COMPLETION of the one just proven — carry equal power from the stereo field (pan) into time (crossfade). A linear crossfade sags in the middle exactly as a linear pan dips at center; ALES11 already answers it. Chosen over stereo metering / balance-width as the move that finishes the equal-power story across both axes.
think The crux is a recognition, not new arithmetic: a crossfade IS the equal-power pan swept across the overlap. Position across the field and position through a time overlap are one parameter, so the outgoing/incoming weights are ALES11's split read at each overlap sample — the proven law REUSED, not re-derived.
think To reuse cleanly I made one additive change to power.rye: a pub `split(pos, den) [2]u32` wrapping the private `weights`, named for the crossfade so the time axis reads exactly the pan the field would. Additive (tier-3 living code); ALES11's public surface only grows, the pan witness re-runs GREEN.
think Because the two weights already satisfy constant power (out_power + in_power = den², out² + in² ≤ den² within the isqrt bound), the crossfade owes fall straight out: pure-outgoing head + pure-incoming tail (seamless splice), and a −3 dB equal-power center (0.707·den) where linear dips to 0.5·den. The sum is ALES3's mixer discipline unchanged — wide i64, saturate once (timeline.saturate).
obs GREEN on first build across six blocks. Endpoint asserts inside the loop (i==0 → pure out, i==den → pure in) hold on metal. The self-cross test proves the equal-power lift positively: every interior sample ≥ the endpoint level and the center is the peak — the opposite of a linear sag. tame_style_check bans clean, power witness re-runs GREEN (split is additive), crossfade errors reuse timeline.EditError so no new error name.
obs Honest scope kept explicit: the overlap runs across sample indices within one shared clip bound; a routing/loudness curve, no psychoacoustic or electrical claim; purely local, no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real speaker. No custody gate reached. Live clock read 123255, monotonic after ALES11's 122502.
loom witness=ales_crossfade_witness cases=6 build=first_green tame=clean center_amp=700 linear_amp=500 power_regreen=1
